# Console syntax-block test — an accordion widget whose body is a {{syntax:lang}}
# block over several lines.  A widget measures and colorizes its body LINE BY LINE,
# so a block's tags reach the rendering pass separately: the end tag alone used to
# throw (openSyntax(null) — a rule that merely CONTAINS the "syntax:" prefix, such
# as /syntax:python, was taken for a language), and the border a widget draws through
# the block's lines came out as literal tag text.
#
#   bin/metatron-console --steps bin/test/console-syntax-block.steps
#   bin/metatron-console --cwd repo --steps bin/test/console-syntax-block.steps
#
# The body text is asserted after a forced redraw (alt+w): the echoed command line
# carries the same literals, so a needle matched against the whole transcript would
# pass even when the widget drew nothing.  Border glyphs are NOT matched — this pty
# draws the right border as "|" and the left as "│" — and neither is colour: run with
# --cwd repo (a cwd holding conf/nanorc) to have the block colorized at all, since
# conf/nanorc is resolved relative to the vm's working directory.
#
# Two characters cannot appear in a SEND line here: ";" separates steps and "#"
# starts a comment, so the sample is Python rather than Java.

WAIT_CONSOLE

# the widget floats (its title bar is render-only: the echo never contains it)
MARK block
SEND accordion_widget::[title=>'syntax block',body=>"{{syntax:python}}class Sample:\n    ANSWER = 42\n\ndef helper(value):\n    return value * ANSWER\n{{/syntax:python}}",style=>[anchor=>top_left,width=>64,height=>16]].display()
WAIT_SINCE block ┌ syntax block 25
SILENT block task threw
SILENT block cannot invoke
SILENT block unmatched

# focus it: the surface redraws the widget, so the body prints AFTER the echo and a
# body-text needle matches the render and nothing else
MARK redraw
KEY alt+w
WAIT_SINCE redraw class sample 25
WAIT_SINCE redraw def helper 25
WAIT_SINCE redraw return value 25

# the redraw shows code, never the tags
MARK tags
SLEEP 1
SILENT tags {{syntax:python}}
SILENT tags {{/syntax:python}}
